# RFC#45 chunk 4 — multi-seed tree learning at e10/e11
# Sample-fraction jitter + predictor-order shuffle (paired A/B/C bench)
#
# Change ID (jj):                          zvnwxrmqxyyklozswtmqkzqskquovqml
# (commit hash visible via `git log` after push; see CHANGELOG.md entry too)
# Rebase parent (origin/main):             16a521a3a5d2
# Chunk-3 baseline reference:              a8fbd36020e8
# Chunk-2 (multi-seed wiring):             d4f2e2822600
#
# Workspace:    jxl-encoder--e10-chunk4 (jj-colocated sibling of main repo)
# Bench host:   AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (16C/32T, 128 GB), Linux 6.6 WSL2
# Build:        cargo build -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'std parallel parallel-tree-learning' --example e10_e11_multiseed_chunk4_ab
# Run cmd:      SAMPLES=2 THREADS=8 ./target/release/examples/e10_e11_multiseed_chunk4_ab
# Corpus:       /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/
# Images:       1025469.png, 1044329.png, 1189261.png, 1279330.png, 1418519.png
# Efforts:      e9 (single-seed), e10 (2 seeds), e11 (4 seeds)
# Samples:      2 per (image, effort) cell (paired sample-major interleave)
#
# Variance dimensions added on top of chunk 3:
#   1. derive_seeded_sample_fraction(seed) - per-seed absolute tree_sample_fraction
#      cycled by seed%4 over [None, Some(0.40), Some(0.60), Some(0.70)].
#      Seed 0 keeps the canonical profile fraction (None -> byte-identical).
#      Applied via stride_for_seeded_sample_fraction() so it composes cleanly
#      with chunk-3's derive_seeded_stride (chunk-4 takes precedence).
#   2. derive_seeded_predictor_order(seed) - per-seed permutation of the 14
#      CANDIDATE_PREDICTORS array (canonical / strong-first / directional-first
#      / full-reverse). Affects greedy ID3's strict-< tie-break in
#      find_best_predictor. Set equality preserved -> every per-seed tree
#      remains spec-valid; the chunk-2 token-cost picker chooses among them
#      on equal terms.
#
# Hash-lock invariant: 36/36 hash_lock_features tests pass at e <= 9
# (tree_learn_seeds = 1 for e <= 9 -> seed-0-only path, byte-identical).
#
# Bench format (TSV):
#   image    effort    sample_idx    bytes    sha-4    wall_ms
#
# A/B/C bytes summary (per-image, mean over 2 samples; deterministic encoder so
# samples are identical bytes within a cell):
#
#   image           e9        e10       e11       delta10%  delta11%
#   1025469.png     231695    231461    231461    -0.10     -0.10
#   1044329.png     330198    330499    330499    +0.09     +0.09
#   1189261.png     303156    303864    303864    +0.23     +0.23
#   1279330.png     208471    207123    207123    -0.65     -0.65
#   1418519.png     165481    165275    163908    -0.12     -0.95
#   --------------------------------------------------------------
#   TOTAL           1239001   1238222   1236855   -0.06%    -0.17%
#
# Honest chunk-3 -> chunk-4 comparison (per-image bytes, same 5-image corpus):
#
#   image           effort    chunk3_B  chunk4_B  delta_B   delta%
#   1025469.png     e9        231695    231695    +0        +0.000
#   1025469.png     e10       231461    231461    +0        +0.000
#   1025469.png     e11       231461    231461    +0        +0.000
#   1044329.png     e9        330198    330198    +0        +0.000
#   1044329.png     e10       330499    330499    +0        +0.000
#   1044329.png     e11       327001    330499    +3498     +1.070
#   1189261.png     e9        303156    303156    +0        +0.000
#   1189261.png     e10       303864    303864    +0        +0.000
#   1189261.png     e11       302399    303864    +1465     +0.484
#   1279330.png     e9        208471    208471    +0        +0.000
#   1279330.png     e10       207027    207123    +96       +0.046
#   1279330.png     e11       207027    207123    +96       +0.046
#   1418519.png     e9        165481    165481    +0        +0.000
#   1418519.png     e10       165275    165275    +0        +0.000
#   1418519.png     e11       164133    163908    -225      -0.137
#
#   TOTAL @e9       1239001   1239001   +0        +0.000%
#   TOTAL @e10      1238126   1238222   +96       +0.008%
#   TOTAL @e11      1232021   1236855   +4834     +0.392%
#
# Net finding (HONEST): chunk-4 REGRESSES at e11 by +0.39% on this 5-image
# corpus vs chunk-3, despite adding two more variance dimensions. At e10
# the net is a wash (+0.008%). The new sample-fraction / predictor-order
# perturbations displace some of chunk-3's winning split-threshold +
# property-order perturbations on 1044329 and 1189261 at e11. Only one
# cell (1418519@e11) improves over chunk-3 (-0.137%).
#
# Interpretation:
#   - Variance dimensions are NOT additive on this 5-image subset.
#   - With 4 seeds at e11 the budget is fixed; adding more variance dimensions
#     and cycling them mod-4 changes WHICH 4 candidate trees are evaluated,
#     not how many. Chunk-3's 4 perturbations happened to hit better minima
#     on 2/5 images than chunk-4's recombined set.
#   - Possible follow-ons: (a) restore the chunk-3 dimensions and add chunk-4
#     dimensions only at seed indices beyond 3 (requires >4 seed budget,
#     i.e., a new effort tier or env-gated tuning); (b) factor-of-2 expansion
#     to 6 or 8 seeds at e11 to fit all variance dimensions independently;
#     (c) per-image dispatch — accept chunk-3 won where chunk-4 lost.
#   - Larger corpus sweep needed before promoting chunk-4 over chunk-3.
#
# Hash-lock outcome: PASS — 36/36 hash_lock_features tests at e <= 9.
#                    Bytes byte-identical at e <= 9 vs origin/main and vs
#                    chunk-3 a8fbd36020e8 (all 5 images, both efforts).
